  # (0.3.1 C5) The CROSS-EMIT row: TEKO_TARGET names a target this host may be able to BUILD but
  # cannot EXECUTE. R3 says emit normally; C5 says report "emitted, not executed" and skip the run
  # instead of failing on an exec of a foreign-format binary. The RUN is honest-skipped by
  # cross_note_for_name (the same classification the build's own report uses) while `Then object
  # well-formed` still asserts the emitted object IS the requested format — which is the whole point
  # of a cross build. On a host with no cross toolchain the row skips earlier, at
  # target_toolchain_skip_reason.
  Scenario: own_cross_x86_64_windows_emits_coff_and_skips_the_run (0.3.1 C5 — emitted, not executed)
    Given target = "x86_64-windows"
    Given source = "cases/cross_exit42.tks"
    When built and run
    Then exit = 42
    Then object well-formed

  # (0.3.1 C5) The host os-arch spelled EXPLICITLY: the reproduced-good path of the motivating bug
  # (an explicit TEKO_TARGET made the whole vertical work, exit 42).
  #
  # IT NAMES `host-os-arch`, NOT `x86_64-linux` (owner ruling 2026-07-27: *"precisa ensinar o
  # regressor a entender diferentes OSes e arquiteturas para variar um mesmo teste"*). The subject of
  # this row is that a target spelled OUT works — not that the target is x86_64. Hardcoding the
  # architecture made it a CROSS row on every host that is not x86_64-linux, where it honest-skipped
  # instead of running: the same test, deleted by a constant. The token resolves to whatever os-arch
  # this host natively builds, so the row RUNS on every host and still exercises the
  # explicitly-spelled path (which the plain `host` sentinel, exporting no `TEKO_TARGET` at all, does
  # not). The rows above keep their explicit `x86_64-windows` / `wasm32-wasi` names because for THEM
  # the architecture IS the subject, and an honest skip without the cross toolchain is correct.
  Scenario: own_explicit_host_os_arch_runs (0.3.1 C5 — the reproduced-good path)
    Given target = "host-os-arch"
    Given source = "cases/cross_exit42.tks"
    When built and run
    Then exit = 42
    Then object well-formed


